Z||000000||CoolBlue87GT||12-06-2001||12:10 PM||||From morning paper  (was long story, made short)<P>Titled Car trunk search debate opens in Supreme Court<P>TALLAHASSEE (AP)<BR>Almost five years ago, a Clearwater police officer pulled over Kellen Betz over because his Pontiac Fiero had a headlight out.<P>On Wednesday, lawyers were in Florida Supreme Court arguing whether the veteran officer should have searched Betz's trunk after smelling a marijuana cigarette through the cars open window.<P>The officer found a bag of marijuana on Betz and then discovered more in a metal box in a briefcase in the trunk.....<P>....Assistant public defender representing Betz said, We argue that there was never probable cause to search the trunk in the first place.<P>--------------------------------------------------------<P>Well, I guess we better fix those headlights !!!  ||||reg||6
