Z||000013||maryjane||12-07-2001||12:26 AM||||I used to have a weblink about a Maryland case. It more or less said that the search could not be conducted in the same stop as a non-drug related stop. The officer would have to do the traffic ticket write-up, say " you can go" or "You're free to go",<BR>then, ask for permission to search the car. <BR>In other words, you can't stop someone for a tailight being out, then proceed to search the car just because you suspect some drugs.<P>------------------<BR>Don't be so open minded  your brains fall out!||||reg||1
